<section class="ss-c-demo__section">
    <h2>Guide Mixins</h2>
    <p>Visual overlay mixins for development and layout debugging.</p>

    <h3>guide--baseline</h3>
    <p>Renders a baseline grid overlay for vertical-rhythm debugging.</p>

    <pre class="ss-c-code-block">@include guide--baseline</pre>

    <pre class="ss-c-code-block"><code>// Apply to a layer element
.guide-overlay {
    @include guide--layer;
    @include guide--baseline;
}</code></pre>

    <h3>guide--graph / guide--graph_centered</h3>
    <p>Renders a graph (column) grid overlay. The <code>_centered</code> variant aligns the grid to the viewport
        center.</p>

    <pre class="ss-c-code-block">@include guide--graph<br>@include guide--graph_centered</pre>

    <pre class="ss-c-code-block"><code>.guide-overlay {
    @include guide--layer;
    @include guide--graph_centered;
}</code></pre>

    <h3>guide--margin</h3>
    <p>Highlights margin areas for layout inspection.</p>

    <pre class="ss-c-code-block">@include guide--margin</pre>

    <pre class="ss-c-code-block"><code>.guide-overlay {
    @include guide--layer;
    @include guide--margin;
}</code></pre>

    <h3>guide--layer</h3>
    <p>Base layer mixin -- positions the overlay element fixed across the viewport. Combine with one of the visual
        guides above.</p>

    <pre class="ss-c-code-block">@include guide--layer</pre>

    <h3>guide--centered</h3>
    <p>Centers a guide horizontally within its container.</p>

    <pre class="ss-c-code-block">@include guide--centered</pre>
</section>
